Conjugation by a Scott map after and a Scott map before sends a Scott endomap to the composite of the first, the endomap, and the second. `conjMapFun` is that composite as a bare function, and `conjMap.fun_apply` says evaluating it at a point is the outer map applied to the endomap applied to the inner map. `conjMap.preservesDirectedSup` says this composite preserves directed suprema: the two sides agree at an arbitrary point, evaluation at the image of that point under the inner map preserves directedness, and the outer map preserves the resulting directed supremum. `conjMap` is the same conjugation bundled as a Scott map, with that preservation as its continuity. `conjMap.apply` is the bundled map evaluated at a point, which agrees with the underlying conjugation.
